{"title": "[CT-243] Allocate loaded tolls to customer at 8-mile threshold", "description": "Fix `allocate_toll_costs` billing loaded tolls at the 8-mile deadhead boundary to the carrier. The default `short_loaded_miles` threshold was 9 instead of the documented 8 miles; the comparison was already inclusive. A loaded $9.00 segment over exactly 8.00 miles now allocates $9.00 customer / $0.00 driver / $0.00 carrier. Loaded segments below 8 miles still settle as local repositioning, and other segment/lane cases are unchanged.

Tests run: full `pytest tests` suite, 386 passed (1 pre-existing PytestCollectionWarning). Added `test_loaded_segment_at_eight_miles_bills_customer`, `test_loaded_segment_just_over_eight_miles_bills_customer`, and `test_custom_short_loaded_threshold_is_inclusive`; existing 7.99-mile short-load test unchanged. CHANGELOG updated under `## Unreleased`.

Risk: low", "status": "ready"}
